## Third-party services used at build time (not redistributed)

- **Offline TTS** (Kokoro `am_michael`, with the corrected Frame 6 line
  synthesized by `espeak-ng`): used locally at build time from the
  repository's own public script. No credentials are used and no
  visitor-runtime dependency exists; the synthesized audio is baked into the
  MP4.
- **Mermaid / @mermaid-js/mermaid-cli** (Apache-2.0): build-time diagram
  rendering only; no Mermaid code is shipped to visitors.

## Fonts, scripts, and media from third parties

None. The site uses system font stacks only, ships no third-party
visitor-runtime JavaScript, references no remote fonts, and redistributes no stock
photography, icon sets, or media.

## Privacy-related assets

The site sets no cookies, runs no analytics, and collects no visitor data;
the quality gate in `scripts/check_site_quality.py` enforces the absence of
known tracking patterns.

## Local media source disposition

`media-src/stateport-overview/` is local untracked build source, not an
executable or published Pages asset. Its source manifest records the final
capture inputs, mascot provenance, `mp4Present: true`, and the local MP4
digest without making a publication or acceptance claim.
